{"kind":"request","text":"Make recording a large merge succession scale with the number of acts plus the log depth, not their product.\n\nhugh asked in chat on 2026-10-14 whether the builder's two-hour `gs land` in artroom was stuck, and approved filing this.\n\nObserved in artroom on 2026-10-14. The builder's `gs land` of the repository-hygiene head (merge 0f1f485d, 724 changed paths) carries 407 retirements and 381 successors, about 788 acts. The local merge finished at 12:13 and the receipt was recorded at 12:24. At 13:35 the process (gs 5876d211) had used 128 CPU-minutes and had appended none of the succession acts. A planner `gs merge` had waited behind it on the meta lock for 50 minutes. The log depth was 40,104 events.\n\nA stack sample shows the cause. `recordMergeSuccession` (cmd/gs/succession.go:83@5876d211) calls `preflightBatchAdmission`, then `runBatch`, and `runBatch` calls `preflightAdmission` (cmd/gs/main.go:2362@5876d211) over the same acts again. For each act, `preflightAdmission` calls `BuildActRequest` (AdmitState, judgeState, judgeDeadBases) and, for each labelled act, `AcceptedActUnderKey`, which goes through `kernel.PriorAct` and `scanHeadInto` to read the whole log. A new `git cat-file --batch` starts about every 5.5 seconds, so each pass takes about 70 minutes before the appends begin.","body":{"conditions":"1. One landing runs admission preflight over a succession batch once, not twice. 2. The prior-act lookup by idempotency key reads the log once per batch, not once per act. 3. Per-act admission judges against one shared snapshot. 4. A test with a succession of hundreds of acts counts git subprocesses or log scans, and goes red if the count grows with the number of acts. 5. An interrupted landing still resumes and replays correctly; an existing or new test pins this. 6. go test ./... passes at the head. 7. The report states the before and after time to record a large succession on a copy of the artroom log, or says plainly what was not measured.","target_head":"5876d2118fa3d9d223dfc923744bc0bb9ef1dfc0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}